<<ad _ad>>


Was spying on your friend and classmate hoping to get some peeks at a private moment weird? Definitely. However, your young, horny brain is too overcome with the possibilities to back out now! You’re sure <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Felix</span> would just find it funny if he discovered you did this… right? <br>
<br>
You turn a corner, quickly moving between two of the houses and exit into the tree line. Avendale rests on a cliffed hill, meaning you have to go through the gate unless you want to try your hand at rock climbing, but once you got back here, you were mostly out of site, as long as you steered clear of any fences armed with alarms. So, you stay as close to the edge of the cliff as you can, using the collection of trees and foliage here as cover, as you make your way to the house <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Felix</span> is staying in. <br>
<br>
<<linkreplace"Continue">>
    You almost miss it, not remembering what it looked like from the back, but eventually recognize the tree whose branch caresses his bedroom window. The light in the room also appears to be on, meaning <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Felix</span> is here! Though this also means you have to be careful. So, you move towards a second tree near the back fence. You had no hope of climbing up the stone fence that lined the back yard, but you could climb this tree and jump to the other. It is honestly insane and hardly worth the effort, <span style="Color: LightGreen">but the image of what <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Felix</span> could be doing right now spurs you forward as you begin to climb!</span> <br>
    <br>
    Thankfully, these trees are wide with low branches, making climbing them pretty easy. Their branches near the top also look sturdy enough to hold you, so once you reach one that peeks into the yard, you take a deep breath before running as best as you can and leaping to the other tree! <br>
    <br>
    You catch it, just barely, and manage to pull yourself up as the tree shakes and leaves ruffle. You creep into the leaves, obscuring yourself until you are sure the coast is clear. <span style="Color: LightGreen">Thankfully, no one comes and you are free to creep towards the window.</span> <br>
    <br>
    You can’t get over how silly this is, climbing trees and jumping from branches just to get a peek at your friend in the privacy of his bedroom. It’s like you were some perverted cartoon character. <span style="Color: Yellow">Though it is pretty exciting, like an adventure, and your heart starts to beat faster when you see the bedroom curtains open just enough to give you a peek at the inside.</span> <br>
    <br>
